  "_comment": "FIX 67 — One secret-name canon. Maps each CANONICAL secret name to its recognized aliases. Shape: {\"CANONICAL\": [\"ALIAS\", ...]}. The canonical name is always the first element of its own alias list when a reader expands it. Consumers (all must read THIS file, never restate their own map): install.sh get_alias_list (bash fallback inlined there stays byte-compatible), check-skill-prereqs.sh search_env_var, key_resolver.py SERVICE_ALIASES, api_key_utils.py KEY_PATTERNS, research_web brave_key_present, capacity.py PROVIDER_PROBE_DEFS, the dispatcher provider key map, kie_generate. Keys stored under ANY alias in the family must resolve in every reader on both platforms (Mac ~/.openclaw/secrets/.env, VPS /data/.openclaw/secrets/.env). Add new aliases here, not in code.",
  "_direction": "Two families are bidirectional by design and both canonical names resolve to the same credential: BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY <-> BRAVE_API_KEY (research_web reads BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY; the secrets store historically holds BRAVE_API_KEY) and OLLAMA_API_KEY <-> OLLAMA_CLOUD_API_KEY (dispatcher and model_router read OLLAMA_CLOUD_API_KEY; install.sh and legacy stores hold OLLAMA_API_KEY). Every other family has one canonical head; aliases are alternates found in the wild.",
